#env
# .env.local holds per-developer values and stays out of the repo. .env.production
# and .env.staging are committed on purpose: they carry only VITE_* values, which
# Vite inlines into the public browser bundle anyway. See the comments in those files.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.production
!.env.staging

# Logs
/logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
lerna-debug.log*

node_modules
dist
dist-ssr
*.local

# Editor directories and files
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
.idea
.DS_Store
*.suo
*.ntvs*
*.njsproj
*.sln
*.sw?

.vite
